#. i18n: file: profilenetworkgeneraloptionsbase4.ui:112
#. i18n: ectx: property (toolTip), widget (QCheckBox, FixPathMtuDiscoveryProblemCheckBox)
#: rc.cpp:3588
msgid ""
"Fixes the path MTU discovery problem by inserting a special firewall rule."
msgstr "Richt dat Padd-MTU-Opdeckproblem, föögt en besünner Nettdiek-Regel in."

#. i18n: file: profilenetworkgeneraloptionsbase4.ui:116
#. i18n: ectx: property (whatsThis), widget (QCheckBox, FixPathMtuDiscoveryProblemCheckBox)
#: rc.cpp:3591
msgid ""
"Problem: TCP connections using the PPTP Client host as a hop in the route "
"(such as via normal routing, NAT or IP masquerading) freeze once they "
"attempt to transfer large amounts of data.\n"
"Diagnosis: path MTU discovery may not be working, due to hosts on the route "
"refusing to forward ICMP fragmentation needed responses."
msgstr ""
"Problem: TCP-Verbinnen, de den PPTP-Client-Reekner as Jumpsteed binnen den "
"Nettweg bruukt (binnen den normalen Nettweg, över NAT oder IP-Maskereren), "
"freert in, wenn se groot Datenmengden överdregen schöölt.\n"
"Oorsaak: Dat Opdecken vun de Padd-MTU funkscheneert villicht nich, wiel "
"Reekners binnen den Nettweg nödig ICMP-Opspleet-Antern nich wiedergeevt."

#. i18n: file: profilenetworkgeneraloptionsbase4.ui:119
#. i18n: ectx: property (text), widget (QCheckBox, FixPathMtuDiscoveryProblemCheckBox)
#: rc.cpp:3595
msgid "Fix path mtu discovery problem"
msgstr "Padd-MTU-Opdeckproblem richten"

#. i18n: file: profilenetworkgeneraloptionsbase4.ui:165
#. i18n: ectx: property (whatsThis), widget (KComboBox, NetworkDeviceComboBox)
#: rc.cpp:3604
msgid ""
"This is the network device which should be used for the tunnel. It is only "
"active if needed. If no selection is made, \"default\" is set, to use the "
"device where the defaultroute points to."
msgstr ""
"Dit is de Nettwarkkoppelsteed, de Du för den Tunnel bruken wullt. Se is "
"bloots anmaakt, wenn dat noot deit. Is nix angeven, warrt \"Standard\" "
"bruukt. Denn warrt de Reedschap för de Steed bruukt, woneem de "
"Standardnettweg henwiest."

